{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_tH5H1vuIeE5ReYXmZGpoIFRS","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\n## post by eMadman on 3 Jul\n\nTrying to reconnect to Intervals.icu is throwing an error:\n\n\n![image1](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/55ce6aedbe10a9988f8bdc5f5a0e348e.png)\n\n## post by Domestique on 3 Jul\n\n\\- Fixed connecting (or reconnecting) to intervals.icu failing with a “Duplicate scope CALENDAR” error — introduced in v3.0.1 alongside the new calendar push. If v3.0.1 showed you that error, just update and connect again.\n\n**Root cause:** intervals.icu allows one scope per area. v3.0.1’s OAuth request sent both `CALENDAR:READ` and `CALENDAR:WRITE`, so intervals.icu rejected the authorize request outright (“Duplicate scope CALENDAR”) — every OAuth connect and reconnect was bricked. Fix: dropped `CALENDAR:READ`; `WRITE` covers the reads.\n\nlet me know if any other bugs occur\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 4 Jul\n\nI just updated (with the Brew method) from 2.4.5 to 3.0.2.\n\nI had been at the end of week 2 in an “event preparation” training plan which was due to finish on 30 August. The update reset the plan back to a generic 12 week “Improve FTP” plan which I had setup right at the beginning when I was just playing around with the software.\n\nI recreated the actual event preparation plan, but obviously, now its starting from scratch with a “base phase” while I had actually just completed it.\n\nAside from the incorrect plan having been reactivated, is there a way to setup a plan and tell the software a starting date in the past? Or to skip an specific section?\n\nThanks.\n\n## post by Domestique on 5 Jul\n\n### Heading link**Upgrade no longer loses your training plan**\n\nUpgrading from a 2.x version could bring back an old, long-replaced plan instead of your current one. Fixed: on first launch the app finds your real plan from the old location, restores it automatically, and shows a notice. All previous files are kept as backups — nothing is deleted.\n\n**If this already happened to you:** just install this update — your original plan comes back on its own. The plan you re-created afterwards is kept in your backups.\n\n### Heading link**Start a plan mid-way — “I’ve been training already”**\n\nNew option when creating or rebuilding a plan: tick “I’ve been training already” and pick the date your training actually started. The plan is laid out over the full runway from that date, the weeks you’ve already completed are marked done, and you enter exactly where you are — no repeating a base phase you already rode. Works for every goal type, and the phase preview shows the same backdated timeline you’ll get.\n\nIncludes everything from v3.0.x: intervals.icu calendar push, heart-rate training mode, race-ready event plans, and the Analysis tab.\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 5 Jul\n\nJust updated to 3.1.\n\nI had to re-establish my original plan from 2.4 as I had already re-created it in 3.0.2\n\nI’m trying to use the new “Ive been training already” option and have found that the plan structure varies significantly depending on which day I select as the start point.\n\nFor example. (my plan end date is 30/8). if I select a start date of 22/6, it generates a plan with 3 weeks of base, 2 weeks of b1, 2 weeks b2, 1 of peek and 2 of taper.\n\nIf I select a start date of 15/6, it simply adds 1 additional week of base.\n\nIf I select 8/6, It goes back to 2 weeks base, 3 weeks B1 and 3 weeks B2, 2 weeks peak, 2 of taper.\n\nI’m not quite seeing why it seems to go backwards and forwards on the weeks for each specific section? Am I missing something?\n\n## post by Domestique on 5 Jul\n\nNot missing anything — that’s the periodization template switching. The planner reserves your taper, then looks at how many working weeks remain. With 8–9 working weeks it uses a compressed program: the build blocks stay fixed (2+2 weeks) and any extra time goes into base, which is why moving from 22/6 to 15/6 just added a base week. At 10 working weeks it switches to the full program — two 3-week builds and a 2-week peak — and base shrinks back because the extra structure absorbs the time. Same thing happens with fresh plans of those lengths; the backdate just makes it visible as you change the date.\n\nIm making an upgrade now, so you can tune it to custom preference.\n\n## post by Domestique on 5 Jul\n\n### Heading link**Shape your own plan**\n\n- **Phase editor** — step your base/build/peak/taper week counts up or down on an interactive timeline (within safe limits), or snap back to the recommended split.\n- **Mid-plan entry** — tell Domestique you didn’t start today: pick your real start date, or let it read your recent rides and place you on the week your fitness is actually on. No repeating a base phase you already rode.\n\n### Heading link**A workout library you can trust**\n\n- **Every session matches its slot by content, not label** — a sprint day gives you sprints, a sweet-spot day stays sweet spot. The two problems a tester hit (a brutal neuromuscular session on an easy day; 700-watt spikes under a “sweet spot” title) are now impossible by construction and pinned by tests.\n- **The whole 4,000+ library was audited** — ~100 mislabelled files reclassified by hand, and the classifier rules that caused the mislabels are fixed so it holds on updates.\n- **“FTP test” now means an FTP test** — 67 of 75 “FTP test” files weren’t tests; reclassified. The real 20-minute test gains its 5-minute depletion effort.\n- **~30 new sessions** — 30/15, 40/20 and 15/15 microburst VO2 ladders (2/3/4-set), over-unders, sweet-spot builds, and a proper 2×8-minute field test.\n\n### Heading link**Test your FTP your way**\n\n- **Choose ramp or 20-minute, per test** — a side-by-side chooser shows each option’s power profile and honest pros/cons (ramp is quick but reads high for punchy riders; 20-minute is accurate but pace-sensitive). Pick a card and the workout swaps.\n- **Your FTP is read from the effort itself** — the ramp takes your best _sustained_ minute on the ramp (a stray warm-up sprint can’t inflate it), the 20-minute trims a finish kick, and you approve the suggested number.\n\n### Heading link**Train to your own numbers**\n\n- **Cap short intervals to your measured power (opt-in)** — hold a workout’s short, very-hard efforts to what you can actually produce, grounded in critical-power research and your real numbers, approved per workout.\n\n### Heading link**Under the hood**\n\n- Regenerate / add-race / weekly recalc keep every plan setting (distribution, custom bands, races, backdated start). Race days and your completed/moved sessions survive a recalc. First-run setup polish (inline validation, native folder picker, prefill tags).\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 6 Jul\n\nThanks for the update.\n\nA couple of issues:\n\n1. Updating via brew currently fails with a 404 error (downloading the DMG directly works fine) :\n\n\n“Error: platypus45/tap/domestique: Download failed on Cask ‘domestique’ with message: Download failed: https://github.com/platypus45/domestique/releases/download/v3.2.2/Domestique-v3.2.2.dmg\n\n\ncurl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404”\n2. The plan generated workouts don’t always follows the available time. I consistently get 90+ minute sessions scheduled on days with 60 minutes availability.\n3. I had one instance when I tried to reflow a workout multiple times but it always gave me the same alternative.\n\nThanks!\n\n## post by Domestique on 6 Jul\n\n## Heading link**Fixed**\n\n- **Workouts now always fit the time you gave the planner.** If you set a day to 60 minutes, you could still find a 90-minute session on it — the cap was enforced on the main selection path but leaked through several side doors (variety swaps, weekly load redistribution, phase-variety fills). Every path now honours your per-day limit, with one final safety clamp behind them all.\n- **Reshuffle no longer repeats itself.** On slots with few same-length alternatives, “Reshuffle (try another)” could offer the same workout on every click. After a few attempts it now also reaches for slightly shorter workouts — never longer than your day allows.\n- **Updating via Homebrew works again.** `brew upgrade domestique` had failed with a 404 since v3.2.1 (the release file was named differently from what the formula expects). Fixed for the affected releases too — no action needed on your side.\n\n## Heading link**Improved**\n\n- **Recalculated plans keep their variety guarantees.** The automatic weekly recalculation quietly skipped the rules that guarantee over-unders, sprints and short-VO2 work in every build phase. They now run on every recalculation, and your completed or hand-moved sessions are never touched.\n- **Profile safety:** switching rider profiles while ride power data downloads in the background can no longer file that data under the wrong profile.\n\n## post by eMadman on 10 Jul\n\n## post by Sebastian\\_Brooks on 11 Jul\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 12 Jul\n\n## post by Domestique on 12 Jul\n\n## post by Domestique on 13 Jul\n\n## post by Sebastian\\_Brooks on 13 Jul\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 13 Jul\n\n## post by Domestique on 14 Jul\n\n## post by Domestique on 14 Jul\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 17 Jul\n\n16 days later\n\n\n## post by Lapo\\_Nustrini on 2 Aug"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Подтверждено. Теперь у меня полная картина. Выяснил три независимые причины:\n\n1. **Кнопка Connect → 401**: в `static/app.js:28` это обычная ссылка `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. Браузерная навигация не несёт заголовок `Authorization` (токен живёт в localStorage и прикрепляется только обёрткой `fetch` в `api()`), а сервер требует его (`server.py:190`) — отсюда 401 у всех.\n2. **Authorize → 400 invalid_request**: в `config.py:11` запрошены и `ACTIVITY:READ`, и `ACTIVITY:WRITE` (и то же для CALENDAR). По [документации/форуму Intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/domestique-a-free-open-source-science-based-cycling-training-app/130388?page=3) провайдер допускает **один scope на область** (WRITE подразумевает READ); дубликат области → authorize отклоняется. Сентябрьский успех Rivera был со scope без дубликатов (`ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`), а 2026-10-02 добавили пары READ+WRITE — и всё сломалось.\n3. **Протухание через час**: Intervals.icu [не выдаёт ни `refresh_token`, ни `expires_in`](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759) — токен живёт, пока атлет его не отзовёт. А `server.py` выдумывал TTL 3600 с (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), через час помечал соединение «expired» и требовал переподключения.\n\nВношу правки:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_pqawN2Cq1qVN6gjCQee9FjqN","function":{"name":"TodoList","arguments":"{\"todos\":[{\"title\":\"Fix SCOPES: one scope per area (config.py)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"title\":\"auth_init returns JSON url; SPA navigates with Bearer\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Remove fabricated 1h expiry; handle 401 as revocation\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"End-to-end test with local fake Intervals server\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Write causes to ANSWER.md\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}"}}]}
